forest_onboard: Hey CS/Eng — onboarding smoke test failing. After a scale-up to 60 ephemeral workers we see a burst of 429s on /v1/complete and /v1/embeddings. Happens only immediately after deploys. Any quick ideas?

kevin_cs: Sorry about that. Are your workers doing a preflight/prefetch on start? Which SDK and auth mode?

forest_onboard: Node SDK 1.4.4, using ephemeral project keys from our auth proxy. Each worker calls client.prefetch() during init, no startup jitter.

amal_eng: That lines up with a preflight fanout to our auth endpoint. Quick mitigations: 1) add a randomized startup jitter (0-8s) so workers don't all prefetch at once, 2) enable the SDK's ephemeral token cache so workers reuse tokens instead of hitting preflight each boot, 3) add a single-flight lock so only one in-process fetch happens when cache miss occurs.

nora_se: Also add a small retry on 429 with exponential backoff + jitter. Example pseudo: ```js
async function callWithRetry(fn){
  let b=150;
  for(let i=0;i<6;i++){
    try { return await fn(); } catch(e){
      if(e.status===429) await sleep(b + Math.floor(Math.random()*b));
      else throw e;
      b = Math.min(10000, b*2);
    }
  }
}
```And set keepAlive=true and maxConnections to reuse HTTP/2 streams.

amal_eng: On our side we can temporarily enable preflight coalescing for your tenant and bump the preflight window to reduce immediate failures while you roll changes. Want that?

forest_onboard: Yes please flip coalescing for 4h while we patch. We'll add jitter + single-flight + cache today.

ops-bot: feature preflight_coalesce enabled for tenant forest_onboard until ts=2812349079.

forest_onboard: Quick update after changes: enabled SDK token cache, added 0-6s splay, and single-flight fetch. Post-deploy the 429s dropped from ~35% of requests to <2%. Sample logs: ```log
[2812345680] worker/4 splay=3.1s prefetch: cache miss -> fetched
[2812345685] worker/9 prefetch: cache hit token_age=5s
[2812345690] complete:200 latency=160ms
```Thanks — huge improvement.

kevin_cs: Great. I'll send a short runbook with recommended flags: ephemeralCache:true, singleFlight:true, startupSplay:0-8s, keepAlive:true, maxConnections:12, retry{base:150ms,max:10s,jitter:true}. Also include steps to request a permanent preflight quota bump if you expect many simultaneous cold boots.

forest_onboard: Please keep the coalesce flag on for 24h while we run a larger canary and upgrade to SDK 1.4.6 tomorrow. We'll paste a postmortem with timings and config afterwards. Thanks everyone :pray:
